CM_ BU_ SBG "2x SBG Ellipse-D (ELLIPSE-D-G4A3-B2, P/N 100-2425: Land Air INS, dual-antenna GNSS RTK, CAN) on Telemetry CAN, front + rear. Frame layouts, scaling and signedness are copied from SBG's official sbgCan.dbc (github.com/SBG-Systems/sbgECom, can/sbgCan.dbc) and checked against its doc/canProtocol.md; payloads are little-endian. Only the IDs are MUR's: SBG ships every CAN message disabled, and both units are remapped into the 0x220-0x22F block mur_telemetry_can.dbc reserves - front 0x220-0x225 (0x226-0x227 spare), rear 0x228-0x22D (0x22E-0x22F spare). The relative order follows SBG's default IDs. This file is only true while the units are configured to match (sbgCenter: Input/Output > CAN bus Normal @ 1000 kbit/s + IDs; Data Output > the six messages below at their GenMsgCycleTime rates, everything else off). Position/velocity are the Navigation (EKF) outputs, not GNSS1. MUR ADDITION (PROVISIONAL): ID plan pending telemetry team sign-off.";
CM_ BO_ 544 "SBG_ECAN_MSG_STATUS_03 (SBG default ID 0x102), front unit. Bytes 4-5 are HEAVE_STATUS (ship-motion status, meaningless on a car) - left undefined.";
CM_ SG_ 544 SBG_FRONT_SolMode "SOLUTION_STATUS bits 0-3: EKF solution mode. Nothing but NavPosition means position/velocity are trustworthy.";
CM_ SG_ 544 SBG_FRONT_SolAidingFlags "SOLUTION_STATUS bits 8-31: aiding-used flags, SBG_ECOM_SOL_* bit N maps to bit N-8 here (e.g. bit 11 GPS1_POS_USED -> bit 3, bit 27 ALIGN_VALID -> bit 19). See sbgECom doc/binaryMessages.md SOLUTION_STATUS.";
CM_ BO_ 545 "SBG_ECAN_MSG_UTC_0 (SBG default ID 0x110), front unit. TimeStamp is time since the unit powered up; GpsTow is GPS time of week - use it to line up the two units and other logs.";
CM_ BO_ 546 "SBG_ECAN_MSG_IMU_ACCEL (SBG default ID 0x121), front unit. Calibrated accelerometer, sensor body frame.";
CM_ BO_ 547 "SBG_ECAN_MSG_IMU_GYRO (SBG default ID 0x122), front unit. Calibrated gyro, sensor body frame.";
CM_ BO_ 548 "SBG_ECAN_MSG_EKF_POS (SBG default ID 0x134), front unit. WGS84 latitude/longitude from the INS solution; invalid until SolMode = NavPosition.";
CM_ BO_ 549 "SBG_ECAN_MSG_EKF_VEL_NED (SBG default ID 0x137), front unit. INS velocity in the North/East/Down frame, not the car frame.";
CM_ BO_ 552 "SBG_ECAN_MSG_STATUS_03 (SBG default ID 0x102), rear unit - same layout as SBG_Front_Status.";
CM_ BO_ 553 "SBG_ECAN_MSG_UTC_0 (SBG default ID 0x110), rear unit - same layout as SBG_Front_Utc.";
CM_ BO_ 554 "SBG_ECAN_MSG_IMU_ACCEL (SBG default ID 0x121), rear unit - same layout as SBG_Front_Accel.";
CM_ BO_ 555 "SBG_ECAN_MSG_IMU_GYRO (SBG default ID 0x122), rear unit - same layout as SBG_Front_Gyro.";
CM_ BO_ 556 "SBG_ECAN_MSG_EKF_POS (SBG default ID 0x134), rear unit - same layout as SBG_Front_EkfPos.";
CM_ BO_ 557 "SBG_ECAN_MSG_EKF_VEL_NED (SBG default ID 0x137), rear unit - same layout as SBG_Front_EkfVelNed.";

